.TH "ELEMENT.MOUSEUP_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Element.mouseup_event \- Element: mouseup event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]mouseup\f[B]\f[R] event is fired at an \f[CR]Element\f[R]
when a button on a pointing device (such as a mouse or trackpad) is
released while the pointer is located inside it.
.PP
\f[CR]mouseup\f[R] events are the counterpoint to \f[CR]mousedown\f[R]
events.
.PP
This behavior is different from \f[CR]pointerup\f[R] events.
When using a physical mouse, \f[CR]mouseup\f[R] events fire whenever any
button on a mouse is released.
\f[CR]pointerup\f[R] events fire only upon the last button release;
previous button releases, while other buttons are held down, don\(cqt
fire \f[CR]pointerup\f[R] events.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqmouseup\(dq, (event) => { })

onmouseup = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]MouseEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]UIEvent\f[R] and \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
See \f[CR]mousemove\f[R] event for example code.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
